# operator overloading
- allows user-defined objects to interoperate with inflix operators such as + | or unary operators lie - and ~

python rules:
- you cannot overload operators for the built-in types
- cannot create new operators, only overload existing ones
- few operators cannot be overloaded: is, and, or, not

Overloading unary operators (+ - ~):
- implement special method with just one argument: self - special methods are __neg__, __pos__, __invert__ 
- always return a new object!

Inflix operators -- a larger list of special methods (see table on page 397)
Rich comparison operators -- similar list of forward and reverse methods
Augmented assignment -- e.g += __iadd__ -- should always return self
